<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>name</key>
	<string>Fun</string>
	<key>scopeName</key>
	<string>source.fun</string>
	<key>fileTypes</key>
	<array>
		<string>fn</string>
	</array>
	<key>patterns</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>include</key>
			<string>#comments</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>include</key>
			<string>#strings</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>include</key>
			<string>#numbers</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>include</key>
			<string>#operators</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>include</key>
			<string>#typeDeclarations</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>include</key>
			<string>#genericTypes</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>include</key>
			<string>#types</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>include</key>
			<string>#customTypeReferences</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>include</key>
			<string>#functions</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>include</key>
			<string>#booleans</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>include</key>
			<string>#keywords</string>
		</dict>
	</array>
	<key>repository</key>
	<dict>
		<key>operators</key>
		<dict>
			<key>patterns</key>
			<array>
				<dict>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>keyword.operator.fun</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>(-&gt;|::)</string>
				</dict>
				<dict>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>keyword.operator.fun</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>(\+\=|\-\=|\*\=|\/\=|\%\=|\=\=|\!\=|\&lt;\=|\&gt;\=|\&amp;\&amp;|\|\||\&lt;\&lt;|\&gt;\&gt;|\+\+|\-\-|\+|\-|\*|\/|\%|\=|\&lt;|\&gt;|\!|\?|\&amp;|\||\^|\~|\.)</string>
				</dict>
				<dict>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>punctuation.separator.fun</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>(;|,|:)</string>
				</dict>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<key>typeDeclarations</key>
		<dict>
			<key>patterns</key>
			<array>
				<dict>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>meta.type.declaration.struct.fun</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\b(compound)\s+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)(\s*&lt;[^&gt;]+&gt;)?</string>
					<key>captures</key>
					<dict>
						<key>1</key>
						<dict>
							<key>name</key>
							<string>keyword.control.fun</string>
						</dict>
						<key>2</key>
						<dict>
							<key>name</key>
							<string>entity.name.type.struct.fun</string>
						</dict>
						<key>3</key>
						<dict>
							<key>name</key>
							<string>entity.name.type.parameters.fun</string>
						</dict>
					</dict>
				</dict>
				<dict>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>meta.type.declaration.enum.fun</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\b(enum)\s+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)(\s*&lt;[^&gt;]+&gt;)?</string>
					<key>captures</key>
					<dict>
						<key>1</key>
						<dict>
							<key>name</key>
							<string>keyword.control.fun</string>
						</dict>
						<key>2</key>
						<dict>
							<key>name</key>
							<string>entity.name.type.enum.fun</string>
						</dict>
						<key>3</key>
						<dict>
							<key>name</key>
							<string>entity.name.type.parameters.fun</string>
						</dict>
					</dict>
				</dict>
				<dict>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>meta.type.declaration.interface.fun</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\b(shape)\s+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)(\s*&lt;[^&gt;]+&gt;)?</string>
					<key>captures</key>
					<dict>
						<key>1</key>
						<dict>
							<key>name</key>
							<string>keyword.control.fun</string>
						</dict>
						<key>2</key>
						<dict>
							<key>name</key>
							<string>entity.name.type.interface.fun</string>
						</dict>
						<key>3</key>
						<dict>
							<key>name</key>
							<string>entity.name.type.parameters.fun</string>
						</dict>
					</dict>
				</dict>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<key>genericTypes</key>
		<dict>
			<key>patterns</key>
			<array>
				<dict>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>meta.type.generic.fun</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\b([A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\s*(&lt;\s*[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*(?:\s*\*+)?(?:\s*,\s*[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*(?:\s*\*+)?)*\s*&gt;)</string>
					<key>captures</key>
					<dict>
						<key>1</key>
						<dict>
							<key>name</key>
							<string>entity.name.type.fun</string>
						</dict>
						<key>2</key>
						<dict>
							<key>name</key>
							<string>entity.name.type.parameters.fun</string>
						</dict>
					</dict>
				</dict>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<key>comments</key>
		<dict>
			<key>patterns</key>
			<array>
				<dict>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>comment.line.double-slash.fun</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>//.*$</string>
				</dict>
				<dict>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>comment.block.fun</string>
					<key>begin</key>
					<string>/\*</string>
					<key>end</key>
					<string>\*/</string>
				</dict>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<key>strings</key>
		<dict>
			<key>patterns</key>
			<array>
				<dict>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>string.quoted.double.fun</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>"([^"\\]|\\.)*"</string>
				</dict>
				<dict>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>string.quoted.single.fun</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>'([^'\\]|\\.)*'</string>
				</dict>
				<dict>
					<key>comment</key>
					<string>Inline raw string: `` `content` `` closed by a single backtick on the same line; a doubled backtick is the one escape, a literal backtick.</string>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>string.quoted.other.fun</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>`(?:``|[^`])*`</string>
				</dict>
				<dict>
					<key>comment</key>
					<string>Multi-line raw string: a backtick left unclosed on its line starts a block. Each continuation line begins (after leading whitespace) with its own backtick marker; the block ends at an explicit single closing backtick (code may follow it on that line) or at the first line with no marker. Markers and doubled-backtick escapes are inner patterns tried first (applyEndPatternLast), so neither is taken for the closer.</string>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>string.quoted.other.multiline.fun</string>
					<key>begin</key>
					<string>`(?=(?:``|[^`])*$)</string>
					<key>end</key>
					<string>`|^(?!\s*`)</string>
					<key>applyEndPatternLast</key>
					<integer>1</integer>
					<key>patterns</key>
					<array>
						<dict>
							<key>match</key>
							<string>^\s*`</string>
						</dict>
						<dict>
							<key>match</key>
							<string>``</string>
						</dict>
					</array>
				</dict>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<key>numbers</key>
		<dict>
			<key>patterns</key>
			<array>
				<dict>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>constant.numeric.fun</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\b(0x[0-9a-fA-F]+|\d+(?:\.\d+)?)\b</string>
				</dict>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<key>types</key>
		<dict>
			<key>patterns</key>
			<array>
				<dict>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>storage.type.fun</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\b(void|raw|num|dec|f32|f64|str|flag|chr|i[1-9][0-9]*|u[1-9][0-9]*)\b</string>
				</dict>
				<dict>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>support.type.fun</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\b(size_t|ptrdiff_t|ssize_t|intptr_t|uintptr_t|int8_t|uint8_t|int16_t|uint16_t|int32_t|uint32_t|int64_t|uint64_t|time_t|clock_t)\b</string>
				</dict>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<key>customTypeReferences</key>
		<dict>
			<key>patterns</key>
			<array>
				<dict>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>entity.name.type.fun</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\b([A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\b(?=\s*(?:\*+)?\s*[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*\b)</string>
				</dict>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<key>functions</key>
		<dict>
			<key>patterns</key>
			<array>
				<dict>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>meta.function.declaration.fun</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\b(fun)\s+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)(\s*&lt;[^&gt;]+&gt;)?\b</string>
					<key>captures</key>
					<dict>
						<key>1</key>
						<dict>
							<key>name</key>
							<string>keyword.control.fun</string>
						</dict>
						<key>2</key>
						<dict>
							<key>name</key>
							<string>entity.name.function.fun</string>
						</dict>
						<key>3</key>
						<dict>
							<key>name</key>
							<string>entity.name.type.parameters.fun</string>
						</dict>
					</dict>
				</dict>
				<dict>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>meta.function.call.fun</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\b(?!use\b|as\b|pub\b|fun\b|closure\b|als\b|compound\b|shape\b|impl\b|enum\b|let\b|const\b|if\b|elif\b|else\b|fit\b|ret\b|for\b|async\b|await\b|fork\b|break\b|continue\b|defer\b|assert\b|panic\b|test\b|sequential\b|fuzz\b|allow\b|expect\b|true\b|false\b|nil\b)([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\b(?=\s*\()</string>
					<key>captures</key>
					<dict>
						<key>1</key>
						<dict>
							<key>name</key>
							<string>entity.name.function.fun</string>
						</dict>
					</dict>
				</dict>
				<dict>
					<key>comment</key>
					<string>A call spelling out its own generic type arguments (`identity&lt;str&gt;(5)`): a lowercase name, a balanced `&lt;...&gt;` (one level of nesting), then `(`. A capitalized name stays a type, so a downcast arm like `Box&lt;num&gt;(b) -&gt;` is never taken for a call.</string>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>meta.function.call.generic.fun</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\b([a-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)(?=\s*&lt;(?:[^&lt;&gt;()]|&lt;[^&lt;&gt;()]*&gt;)*&gt;\s*\()</string>
					<key>captures</key>
					<dict>
						<key>1</key>
						<dict>
							<key>name</key>
							<string>entity.name.function.fun</string>
						</dict>
					</dict>
				</dict>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<key>booleans</key>
		<dict>
			<key>patterns</key>
			<array>
				<dict>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>constant.language.boolean.fun</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\b(true|false)\b</string>
				</dict>
				<dict>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>constant.language.null.fun</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\b(nil)\b</string>
				</dict>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<key>keywords</key>
		<dict>
			<key>patterns</key>
			<array>
				<dict>
					<key>name</key>
					<string>keyword.control.fun</string>
					<key>match</key>
					<string>\b(packed(?=\s+compound\b)|use|as|pub|fun|closure|als|compound|shape|impl|enum|let|const|asm|volatile|arch|if|elif|else|fit|ret|for|async|await|fork|break|continue|defer|assert|panic|test|sequential|fuzz|allow|expect)\b</string>
				</dict>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</dict>
</dict>
</plist>
